+<p>This is a required field which accepts any positive value. The credit limit of an existing customer is changed only by credit control, as the outcome of a credit review, so the limit and the reason for it are always recorded together. An order that would take the customer over their credit limit is held for credit control to release (when the Check Credit Limits system parameter is on).</p>
 
 <h3>Invoice Addressing</h3>
 
@@ -201,6 +201,59 @@
 
 <p>As well as unlimited notes on individual customers, webERP has the functionality to store an unlimited number of notes on groups of customers based on the debtor type field. As with the notes on individual customers , these notes are displayed in order of priority, and can contain a URL as well as the free form note.</p>
 <!-- Help End: Customers -->
+<!-- Help Begin: CreditControl -->
+<h2><a id="CreditControl">Credit Control</a></h2>
+
+<p>Credit control covers credit reviews, stop and watch, overdue reminder letters, interest and late fees, bad debt write-offs and the credit control report. It is for the credit controller, the deputy credit controller and the finance director, who hold the credit control security token (21). The finance director also holds the approval token (22). Sales reps and the sales office do not have these tokens, so they can see the credit status of customers but cannot change a status or a limit.</p>
+
+<h3>Credit reviews</h3>
+
+<p>Open Credit Control from the Accounts Receivable menu and choose the customer. Record a review with its outcome (limit confirmed, raised or reduced, put on watch, put on stop), the new limit, notes and the next review date. The new limit applies at once, and the review is kept in the history of the customer and cannot be changed or deleted. Every customer has a next review date; a new customer gets one automatically, one standard review period away (12 months unless Finance has set otherwise).</p>
+
+<h3>Stop and watch</h3>
+
+<p>Use Change the credit status to put a customer on stop or on watch, or to take them off, with a reason. Each change records who did it and when. While a customer is on stop no order is accepted from the sales office, the customer portal, electronic orders or the XML-RPC API (the web shop), recurring orders are not created, and orders already taken cannot be dispatched or invoiced until credit control releases them on the Credit Control Report. A customer on watch can be supplied; the person taking the order sees a warning, and the orders taken for a customer on watch are listed for credit control.</p>
+
+<h3>Disputed invoices and exemptions</h3>
+
+<p>Tick an invoice as disputed on the Credit Control page and it is not chased and not charged interest until the dispute is settled. A customer can be exempted from interest, from late fees, or from both.</p>
+
+<h3><a id="CreditControlReport">Credit Control Report</a></h3>
+
+<p>Lists the customers due or overdue a credit review, the customers over their credit limit and by how much, and the customers on watch or on stop, with totals in the home currency. It can be limited to one sales person and one currency. It also lists the orders held for credit control or taken for customers on watch or on stop, which credit control can release. The Aged Debtors report shows the credit status, the credit limit and the last reminder stage of each customer.</p>
+
+<h3><a id="CreditControlDunning">Reminder run</a></h3>
+
+<p>Run this weekly. It shows who would get which letter. Untick the customers you do not want to chase this week, for example where a payment has been promised, then send. Letters go by email to the contacts flagged to receive statements. Customers with no email address are listed so that the letter can be posted, and ticking them records the letter as posted. A customer moves up a stage only while still overdue, a customer who paid gets nothing, and the same stage is not sent twice within the minimum number of days. Every reminder is recorded against the customer and appears in the customer portal.</p>
+
+<h3><a id="CreditControlCharges">Month end interest and late fees</a></h3>
+
+<p>At month end open Month End Interest and Late Fees, check the list of what will be charged to whom, and post it. Each charge is posted in the customer currency as a separate, described item on the customer account and the next statement, and to the income accounts Finance chose. A month is never charged twice to the same customer. A charge can be waived, with a reason, on the Credit Control page; the waiver is also posted to the ledger.</p>
+
+<h3><a id="CreditControlWriteOffs">Bad debt write-offs</a></h3>
+
+<p>A write-off is requested for all or part of the unpaid balance of a customer, with a reason. Up to the approval limit it is posted at once; above it the write-off waits on the Approve Write-offs page for the finance director, who cannot approve their own request. A posted write-off is allocated to the oldest unpaid invoices, posts to the bad debt account (at the carrying value of the invoices, so any currency difference is included), and by default puts the customer on stop. The same page reports the write-offs over a period with who did them and who approved them. If a written-off debt is later paid, the receipt is entered as normal and is shown as a credit on the account; recovering the bad debt in the ledger is a manual journal.</p>
+
+<h3><a id="CreditControlApprovals">Approving write-offs</a></h3>
+
+<p>Only holders of the approval token see this page. Approve or reject each write-off with a note.</p>
+
+<h3><a id="CreditControlParameters">Credit control settings</a></h3>
+
+<p>Finance sets the standard review period, the interest rate, the late fee and the days overdue before charging, the write-off approval limit, the general ledger accounts for interest, late fees and bad debts, and the number, timing and wording of the reminder letters. At go-live the credit controller can load the credit status of the customers from the spreadsheet (customer code, status, credit limit, next review date); the customers on the old stop list are put on stop from day one.</p>
+
+<h3><a id="CustomerCreditHistory">Reminders and charges</a></h3>
+
+<p>Shows the reminders sent to a customer, the interest and fees charged to them and their balance. A customer who logs in to the portal sees only their own account. A sales rep sees the credit status, the credit limit and what is overdue only for their own customers.</p>
+
+<h3>Month end reconciliation</h3>
+
+<p>Z_CheckDebtorsControl compares the debtors control account in the general ledger with the customer transactions period by period, including the interest, fees, waivers and write-offs (customer journals), and lists the customer transactions with no ledger entry, and the ledger entries to the control account that have no customer transaction behind them.</p>
+
+<h3>What sales staff need to know</h3>
+
+<p>Watch means the customer can still be supplied but you must speak to credit control before taking an order. Stop means no order can be taken, and no order for the customer can be dispatched or invoiced, until credit control takes the customer off stop or releases the order. Orders that take a customer over their credit limit are saved and held until credit control approves them. Contact credit control about any customer on watch or on stop.</p>
+<!-- Help End: CreditControl -->
 <!-- Help Begin: Shippers -->
 <h2>Shippers</h2>
 
